WEBVTT

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:15.370
"Give back the egg"

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:18.250
If Jack knows where you live,

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:21.870
you can't go back to where
you're staying, can you?

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.080
You'll have to hide somewhere.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:31.040
I'll be happy to serve as your bodyguard!

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.750
I won't let anybody touch you.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:37.290
If anyone tries, I'll murder
them where they stand--

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:41.120
Blood!

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.450
Hey, stop wasting time!

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:48.700
She'll be fine without any help from us.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:56.950
Why don't you two live together?

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:59.540
H-Hell no!

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:01.500
I can't let a woman like her into my room!

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:04.290
I'd like nothing more!

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:10.250
"And my father was born in Kyoto,
and his family name was Ando..."

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:13.250
Looks like his brain got fried.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:17.660
Um, Sherlock is a talented detective,

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:19.790
but I don't know about
his skills as a bodyguard...

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:24.330
What? You didn't know
he was a master of <i>baritsu</i> ?

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:27.250
What's <i>baritsu</i> ?

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:31.580
I see... A master of <i>baritsu</i> ?

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:34.000
Is <i>baritsu</i> strong?

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.040
Incredibly strong!

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:37.750
Or so they say.

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:39.950
"The Legend of Baritsu"

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:39.950
Or so they say.

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:42.120
"A real fighting style for smarty-pants."

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:45.000
<i>Baritsu</i> , the correspondence course!

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:50.120
Okay, get packing!

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:52.250
Do it for Irene!

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:54.410
You can stay here.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:54.870
Come on.

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:55.250
Huh? Why do I...?

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:55.250
Come on.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:57.450
"Give back the egg"
Huh? Why do I...?

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:57.450
Come on.

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:02.330
"Give back the egg"?

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:04.160
What's the egg?

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:09.080
He's after the USB drive.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:10.500
The USB drive?

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.660
Moran's drive.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:17.370
Jack thinks I still have it.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:21.160
But you gave it back to Moran, right?

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:22.250
No.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.830
I gave him the dummy drive.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.750
Whatever's in here is probably...

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:39.580
...a clue to who Jack is.

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:14.830
"That Woman's Pad"

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:20.410
This is comfier than I thought.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:29.540
I can't sleep here either?

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:33.830
Then what about here?

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:48.750
Oh, did you give up on the password?

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:50.540
I'm less interested in what's inside it, and...

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:54.250
...more interested in how you
can use the drive to catch Jack?

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:56.790
Right?

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:01.500
Excuse me.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:05.950
Um... can I use your bath?

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:10.000
I'll keep doing the cleaning like I have been.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.040
I already cleaned.

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:23.160
W-Wow... And it smells good, too...

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:27.950
That's rose scent. My favorite perfume.

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:30.080
Rose?

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:35.370
Want to eat lunch while you're here?

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:42.370
Hey, I told you to put canned mangos on this.

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:44.620
Oh, I'll get them.

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:46.700
Why not take a bite first?

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:58.620
Here's some ponzu sauce for extra flavor.

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:12.450
Hey, mister!

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:16.370
Come join us!

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:18.870
We're throwing water balloons at the drunks!

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:20.330
Divine punishment!

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:29.200
Get a job!

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:36.080
Hey! You jerk!

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:37.120
We demand an apology!

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:38.950
Get down here!

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:38.950
Sorry, sorry.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:40.160
You little shits!

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:40.160
Sorry, sorry.

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:42.120
Get your asses down here!

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:42.120
You want to join in? It's fun.

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:44.330
Sorry! I can't hear you!

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:44.330
You want to join in? It's fun.

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:48.950
Sorry! I can't hear you!

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:48.950
Sorry. I've got somewhere to be.

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:50.660
Bye!

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:57.160
I don't have anywhere to go.

00:06:57.160 --> 00:07:00.620
You can do it... You can do it, Fuyuto!

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:05.750
As soon as I get this, I can be a man!

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:09.200
Kyogoku- <i>san</i> ?

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:13.500
You've got the wrong guy.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:17.120
Um, your money's still in the machine.

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:24.620
You're asking someone
on a date for the first time?

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:25.660
Yes.

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:28.290
But what you were just buying--

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:32.000
I've decided I won't have kids until I'm 32.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:38.620
Until then, I need to prioritize
my time with Maki- <i>chan</i> .

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:41.500
Maki- <i>chan</i> ? The one who
comes here all the time?

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:44.830
Yes. Her, of course.

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:47.750
I didn't know you liked
that type, Kyogoku- <i>san</i> .

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:49.750
Liked what type?

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:54.000
Oh, I guess I do, yes.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.200
So you like this type, too?

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:58.500
Probably?

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:03.120
By the way, do you have
any experience with that type?

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:03.410
No need to worry.

00:08:03.410 --> 00:08:04.870
"My (Fuyuto) Dream"

00:08:03.410 --> 00:08:04.870
No need to worry.

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:13.040
Hey... Can you come with me?

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:16.200
It's no fun doing it by myself.

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:22.830
<i>Jugemu Jugemu Goko-no surikire</i>
<i>Kaijarisuigyo-no Suigyomatsu...</i>

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:27.540
Oh, you're so funny, Kyogoku- <i>san</i> !

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:29.540
That's not true.

00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:35.950
If only I had a wonderful boyfriend like you.

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:37.250
But that'll never happen!

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:41.750
Maki- <i>chan</i> , actually, there's
someplace I want to take you.

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:51.620
I'll be with you until the end.

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:56.160
And the two of them set out into the night...

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:57.910
What is this, even?

00:08:57.910 --> 00:09:01.160
My plan for the night!

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:05.660
You might talk like this, but would Maki- <i>san</i> ?

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:08.450
Of course, this is just one example.

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:15.660
"Love Strategy"

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:15.660
I've run simulations for every possible situation!

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:18.330
The battle is already won!

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:21.620
You've really put some effort into this.

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:24.910
Men are so dumb.

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:27.500
So what about him?

00:09:30.450 --> 00:09:31.870
Not my type, maybe.

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:34.200
Yeah, he's a no go.

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:34.200
Yeah, that's never happening!

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:35.040
What's up?

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:36.120
So there's this new guy...

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:37.910
Hokari Maki- <i>san</i> !

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:39.750
Yes?

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:45.290
Um... actually... well...
I wanted to talk to you.

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:49.500
Um... basically... what I'm saying is...

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:54.660
Martinis and... room keys and...
in and out, and in and out...

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:57.700
Can I go?

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:57.700
And in and out... and in and out...

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:00.580
He wants to ask you out.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:00.580
And in and out... and in and out...

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:03.830
Yes! That is what I was trying to say!

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:05.700
But...

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:07.160
I'm sorry.

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:11.580
He's got more cash than you'd think.

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:13.370
Why not take him for all he's worth?

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:19.000
Where shall we go?

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:23.040
<i>Yes</i> !

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:25.250
My plan worked!

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:27.620
No way!

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:30.580
Oh, no, Sherlock!

00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:35.410
So much!

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:42.870
Hey there.

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:48.910
Welcome.

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:51.040
What are you doing here?

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:54.250
Jack's after me, so I'm staying here.

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:57.450
Okay, I win.

00:10:57.450 --> 00:11:00.330
Jack, huh?

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:10.040
Which should I get?

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:16.200
Hey, Kyogoku- <i>san</i> ?

00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:17.790
Yes?!

00:11:17.790 --> 00:11:21.910
I can't decide, so... I want them all!

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:24.500
Leave it to me, Maki- <i>chan</i> !

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:33.700
Hey, mister, why are you here all the time?

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:34.830
Are you unemployed?

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:36.330
Are you yummy?

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:39.580
It's up to me what I do and where I go.

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:43.330
What are you doing?

00:11:43.330 --> 00:11:47.830
I'm making a database of stray
old guys who live in this area.

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:49.500
What do you mean stray?

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:51.000
I have a home!

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:56.000
I have good news for the poor guy
who's sitting on a bench eating ramen.

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:59.040
I got some <i>rakugo</i> tickets.

00:11:59.040 --> 00:12:01.040
Want to go with Sherlock?

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:02.660
I'll go.

00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:05.790
Fool.

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:08.120
I've only got three tickets.
What do you want?

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:10.750
But we can't leave her alone.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:13.450
Hey, hurry it up.

00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:15.370
I'll be fine.

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:17.450
You go have fun.

00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:19.830
You heard the lady.

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:21.290
Let's go.

00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:25.080
It's dangerous to be alone. I'll stay here.

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:30.500
Hello? Oh, Yoshio?

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:31.660
An accident?

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:33.580
Wait, I'll be right there!

00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:34.660
What's wrong?

00:12:34.660 --> 00:12:36.120
Sorry. Emergency!

00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:37.450
Go without me!

00:12:37.450 --> 00:12:39.370
Is he okay?

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:45.290
Okay, Watson- <i>san</i> , let's go!

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:07.660
So this must be...

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:09.120
It's Jack.

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:18.000
Even the kitchen!

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:19.660
What about the drive?

00:13:23.330 --> 00:13:26.160
It's not safe here, either.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:28.910
What do I do now?

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:30.370
Use this.

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:42.040
Hey, can I take this off?

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:43.200
No.

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:47.290
We can't let anybody see you.

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:51.330
You're going missing for a while.

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:55.250
Is this hideout really safe?

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:57.450
Boss Kaneko recommended it.

00:13:57.450 --> 00:13:59.790
It'll be fine.

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:06.540
It's an old abandoned movie theater
that Kaneko's business used to run.

00:14:06.540 --> 00:14:09.870
He uses it as a shelter
when there's a gang war.

00:14:12.290 --> 00:14:16.870
The only people who know
Irene's hiding here are us three.

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:18.450
Don't tell anybody else.

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:20.000
Of course!

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:25.040
You're well-prepared, huh?

00:14:25.040 --> 00:14:28.540
You'll have everything
you need here to survive.

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:32.700
Sorry for all the trouble.

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:36.620
Oh, but... can I ask for
two or three more things?

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:37.870
"Hair Iron" "Skin Cream" "Lotion" "Razor"
" <i>Dorayaki</i> " "Ceylon Tea" "Week's Worth of Clothes"

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:39.830
"Hair Iron" "Skin Cream" "Lotion" "Razor"
" <i>Dorayaki</i> " "Ceylon Tea" "Week's Worth of Clothes"

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:39.830
That woman...

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:41.450
She doesn't need some of this stuff!

00:14:41.450 --> 00:14:44.830
If you need someone
to go shopping, I can do it.

00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:47.290
No. I'll do it.

00:14:48.910 --> 00:14:51.700
Um... it'd be faster to split up.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:53.250
I'll do it.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:03.700
I can be useful, too, you know!

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:08.250
He just makes me feel so bad
when he talks like that!

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:11.200
Are you listening, Kyogoku- <i>san</i> ?

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:14.370
I've got bigger problems...

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:15.620
You okay?

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:19.830
I'm standing at a crossroads in my life!

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:26.620
You're kidding me.

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:31.790
I'm telling my princess I love her tonight...

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:34.950
But running the simulations
destroyed my stomach!

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:36.450
Kyogoku- <i>san</i> !

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:41.950
Princess? Not prince?

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:43.410
Well, whatever.

00:15:43.410 --> 00:15:46.910
Make sure you don't end up a mark yourself.

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:51.120
She's just going to take him
for all he's worth and abandon him.

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:55.120
Damn, you pawned off
every single thing he gave you?

00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:56.370
No way!

00:15:56.370 --> 00:15:59.200
Hey, you're being loud!

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:01.870
They were all too expensive for me...

00:16:01.870 --> 00:16:04.580
I want a pay pig, too!

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:06.330
Me, too!

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:09.950
But Kyogoku- <i>san</i> 's really
serious and trying his best!

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:13.870
That crazy plan is never
going to get him anywhere!

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:16.950
But she'll feel his passion.

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:19.120
Not a chance.

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:20.700
Hokari Maki- <i>san</i> !

00:16:23.660 --> 00:16:25.330
Kyogoku- <i>san</i> !

00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:31.080
W-Would you please...

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:32.580
Oh, wow! Is this...!

00:16:32.580 --> 00:16:34.120
Could it be...?

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:41.330
Let me hold your hand!

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:42.910
Please!

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:45.950
A diamond just for holding a guy's hand!

00:16:45.950 --> 00:16:48.370
I'd be willing to grab your rod for a diamond!

00:16:51.580 --> 00:16:53.870
Thank you.

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:59.000
I can finally hold Maki- <i>chan</i> 's hand!

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:00.700
Poor bastard...

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:02.660
Kyogoku- <i>san</i> ?

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:06.000
Why are you doing all this for me?

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:08.040
Because--

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:08.040
Are you after my body?

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:11.660
No, not at all!

00:17:11.660 --> 00:17:13.040
Then what is it?

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:18.160
Because... I want you to be my bride?

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:22.950
I can't accept this.

00:17:22.950 --> 00:17:24.910
No...

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:27.120
Maki- <i>chan</i> !

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:32.080
I can only take this after
we know each other more.

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:36.620
Let's date like a real couple.

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:39.250
Maki- <i>chan</i> !

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:40.450
You're kidding me!

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:42.870
Kyogoku- <i>san</i> !

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:46.040
Oh, no! I'm crying!

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:47.700
Be happy together!

00:17:51.160 --> 00:17:52.910
Congratulations!

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:56.250
Thank you, John.

00:17:56.250 --> 00:17:59.750
You take that step, too, just like I did.

00:17:59.750 --> 00:18:03.250
Don't be afraid of failure!

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:07.450
Let's go somewhere
to have a quiet drink, Maki.

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:08.580
Okay!

00:18:13.410 --> 00:18:14.950
That's right!

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:17.450
There's something I can do, too!

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:22.870
Good luck. No idea what you're
talking about, but good luck.

00:18:38.370 --> 00:18:42.080
"I'm going to do what I can
to help protect Irene- <i>san</i> ."

00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:49.500
Nothing out of the ordinary.

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:56.790
I'm so embarrassed...

00:18:59.830 --> 00:19:03.370
Ma... Ma... Maki- <i>chan</i> !

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:12.450
<i>Maki-chan</i> !

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:35.700
Sherlock?

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:39.580
Watson, you go after Irene!

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:55.450
Sherlock!

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:55.450
What's wrong?

00:19:56.830 --> 00:19:59.290
Operation Tug-of-War!

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:00.580
Roger!

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:02.950
Irene- <i>san</i> !

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:05.250
This is the police!

00:20:05.250 --> 00:20:07.200
Jack got Moriarty!

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:14.580
Ready, go!

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:31.580
Oh, that's Daigoro!

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:38.450
You're right! According to our database,
his habitat is Kabukicho Park!

00:20:38.450 --> 00:20:40.080
What about our pay?

00:20:44.540 --> 00:20:46.410
The drive!

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:52.000
If you won't tell me...

00:20:56.580 --> 00:20:57.870
Irene- <i>san</i> !

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:10.410
Irene- <i>san</i> !

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:16.040
It's Jack! Take care of Irene- <i>sensei</i> !

00:21:18.500 --> 00:21:20.620
Irene- <i>san</i> , hang in there!

00:21:25.540 --> 00:21:28.160
I'll call an ambulance!

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:51.370
What happened to Jack?

00:21:56.500 --> 00:22:00.160
Sherlock, Irene is at the
hospital being treated.

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:01.870
She's dead.

00:22:03.500 --> 00:22:07.000
I just got word.

00:22:07.000 --> 00:22:08.660
No...

00:22:08.660 --> 00:22:10.540
That's disappointing.

00:22:14.620 --> 00:22:19.080
The only people who know
Irene's hiding here are us three.

00:22:20.700 --> 00:22:22.540
Moriarty...

00:22:24.500 --> 00:22:28.000
What were you doing there?

00:23:59.830 --> 00:24:00.120
"Now Hiring Psychics"

00:24:00.120 --> 00:24:04.830
"Now Hiring Psychics"

00:24:00.120 --> 00:24:04.830
Watson... Sherlock is in danger...

00:24:04.830 --> 00:24:06.790
"Sherlock's Room" "On BF3. Only window
is behind desk. Watson sleeps on sofa.
Building is 53 years old."
"Sherlock built his <i>rakugo</i> stage himself!"
